The Windows raw-key scan strategy and SQLCipher page implementation are adapted
and independently reimplemented in Python from:
  jackwener/wx-cli-again
  https://github.com/jackwener/wx-cli-again
  commit 077a54cbfe679bda963cd038d8440422907fc797
  src/scanner/windows.rs, src/scanner/mod.rs, src/crypto/mod.rs
  Apache License 2.0; full upstream license: third_party/wx-cli-LICENSE.txt
Changes: keys are never serialized; reads require exact HMAC; bounded read chunks;
lazy page decryption; WAL checksums and transaction commits are verified; no
plaintext database cache, daemon, account-wide export or outgoing messages.

The MMV1 static-anchor discovery and optional master-key capture approach are
informed by:
  qiaodogbear/ChatTrace
  https://github.com/qiaodogbear/ChatTrace
  commit ea7c3986b4fc4fd8c467c5be829a4c954a6fe070
  Copyright (c) 2026 Qiao Xinliang (qiaodogbear)
  MIT License; full upstream license: third_party/ChatTrace-LICENSE.txt
Changes: PE exception metadata determines function bounds; no copied version
offsets, key store, memory dumps or full-database plaintext export.

Protocol references: SQLCipher v4.6.1 src/sqlcipher.c (Zetetic), and the SQLite
WAL file format specification. SQLite documentation is public domain. Reference
material is recorded in docs/RESEARCH.md. No Weixin client code is redistributed.
